-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): the RELATED PROVISIONS (src:3599-4000) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current
-- to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member,
-- or who is self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or
-- weeks they need, how much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission.
--
-- What the related provisions mean to that person. They are the transitional and savings provisions of amending Acts:
-- they say WHICH VERSION of the Act governs a benefit period, a claim or a week (the older text that still applies, or the
-- newer text that applies only from a day), which election the person may still make and by when, and what becomes of an
-- appeal or request that was pending when the appeal bodies changed. The amendments themselves are encoded by the other
-- pieces; the older text that "continues to apply" is not in the deposited texts, so these answers say THAT it governs and
-- WHICH provisions it governs, not what they say.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the
-- person would be asked. The records and the core's types the layer-1 rules expect (a `Period of days`, a `Reason for
-- benefits`, a `Part of the Act`) are built inside each question from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then
-- called; no rule is restated here.
--
-- DAYS THAT ARE NOT IN THE TEXT. An amending Act often fixes a day as "the day on which sections 15, 16 and 21 come into
-- force" or "the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council". Those days are fixed by the amending Act or by an order,
-- not by the deposited texts, so the person (or the form) is asked for them. A different day would change the
-- answer; nothing here supplies one.
--
-- Provisions that have no question here, and why (NOTES.md has the coverage table):
--   * 2008, c. 28, s. 39(3), (4): when an amendment applies to remittances by a prescribed person (a payer of premiums); a
--     claimant remits nothing under it, and the employer's seat is not written in this piece.
--   * 2012, c. 19, s. 251 and 2023, c. 26, s. 664: definitions of bodies; the answers below name the bodies.
--   * 2022, c. 10, s. 406: agreements or arrangements between the Commission and others under Part II; the person holds no claim under them.
--   * 2018, c. 12, s. 292(2): the version of the Regulations (a day, August 11, 2018) used by the questions on ss. 293 to 295.
--   * The amendments not in force (src:4003-4201) change nothing today and have no question.
-- The employer's seat is not written in this piece.

§ `Employment Insurance Act -- related provisions: the claimant's questions`

§§ `Which version of the Act governs my benefit period, claim or week (amendments of 2003 to 2015)`

-- SITUATION: you are asking about a benefit period, a claim or a week from before 2016. For a claim made today the newer
-- text applies and every answer in this group is "yes, the amendment applies".

-- 2003, c. 15, s. 25(1). Sections 15 to 20 and 22 of that Act apply to every week of a benefit period that begins on or
-- after January 4, 2004, and, for a benefit period not yet ended on that day, to the weeks that begin on or after it.
@export Do the amendments in sections 15 to 20 and 22 of the 2003 Act apply to this week of my benefit period (2003, c. 15, s. 25(1))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week you are asking about begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the 2003 amendments in sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to this week of my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) `the week I am asking about began on`

-- 2005, c. 34, s. 56. The repeal of sections 127 and 128 does not affect the validity of a disclosure of information, or of an agreement
-- for making information available, that either Minister named made under those sections.
@export Is a disclosure of information, or an agreement for making information available, that a Minister made under the repealed sections 127 and 128 still valid (2005, c. 34, s. 56)?
GIVEN `it was made under section 127 or 128 of the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure of information, or the agreement for making information available, made under section 127 or 128 of the Employment Insurance Act (the sections that were repealed)?
      `it was made by the Minister of Human Resources Development or the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by the Minister of Human Resources Development, or by the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development?
      `it was valid when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it valid when it was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128 still valid` IS
    `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` `it was made under section 127 or 128 of the Employment Insurance Act` `it was made by the Minister of Human Resources Development or the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development` `it was valid when it was made`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 616. Section 14 as amended applies only to claimants whose benefit period is established on or after
-- April 7, 2013.
@export Does section 14 of the Act as amended in 2012 apply to my benefit period (2012, c. 19, s. 616)?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (the day your claim was made and accepted)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 14 as amended in 2012 apply to my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 616 section 14 as amended by section 604 applies to the claimant` `my benefit period was established on`

-- 2012, c. 27, s. 32. The amended sections 18, 21 and 152.03 apply only to claims because of illness, injury or quarantine
-- for weeks that begin on or after the day sections 15, 16 and 21 of that Act came into force.
@export Do the sickness amendments of 2012 to sections 18, 21 and 152.03 apply to my claim (2012, c. 27, s. 32)?
GIVEN `I am claiming because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `my claim is for the week that began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week of your claim begin?
      `sections 15, 16 and 21 of the 2012 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 15, 16 and 21 of 2012, c. 27 come into force? (the day is in that Act; it is not in the text of the Employment Insurance Act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the 2012 sickness amendments to sections 18, 21 and 152.03 apply to my claim` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 27 s. 32 sections 18, 21 and 152.03 as amended apply to the claim` `my reason` `my claim is for the week that began on` `sections 15, 16 and 21 of the 2012 Act came into force on`
    WHERE
        `my reason` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming because of illness, injury or quarantine`
            THEN `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
            ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- 2012, c. 27, s. 33. Sections 23.2 and 152.061 (care of a critically ill child) apply to a benefit period that begins on or
-- after the day sections 18 and 23 of that Act came into force, and, for one not yet ended on that day, to the weeks
-- that begin on or after it.
@export Do the sections on a critically ill child apply to this week of my benefit period (2012, c. 27, s. 33)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week you are asking about begin?
      `sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 18 and 23 of 2012, c. 27 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 23.2 and 152.061 apply to this week of my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 27 s. 33 sections 23.2 and 152.061 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) `the week I am asking about began on` `sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act came into force on`

-- 2013, c. 35, s. 4. The new paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) do not apply to a week for which the claimant or the
-- self-employed person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or similar institution before the 2013 Act came into force.
@export Are the new rules on weeks of confinement in a jail left out for this week of mine (2013, c. 35, s. 4)?
GIVEN `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week you are asking about begin?
      `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution for that week?
      `the 2013 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2013, c. 35 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the new paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) left out for this week of mine` IS
    `Act RP 2013 c. 35 s. 4 paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) do not apply to the week` `the week I am asking about began on` `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution for that week` `the 2013 Act came into force on`

-- 2014, c. 20, s. 250. Subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) as enacted apply only to sickness claims for weeks that begin on
-- or after the day sections 247 and 248 of that Act came into force.
@export Do the sickness amendments of 2014 to subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) apply to my claim (2014, c. 20, s. 250)?
GIVEN `I am claiming because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `my claim is for the week that began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week of your claim begin?
      `sections 247 and 248 of the 2014 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 247 and 248 of 2014, c. 20 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the 2014 sickness amendments to subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) apply to my claim` IS
    `Act RP 2014 c. 20 s. 250 subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) as enacted apply to the claim` `my reason` `my claim is for the week that began on` `sections 247 and 248 of the 2014 Act came into force on`
    WHERE
        `my reason` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming because of illness, injury or quarantine`
            THEN `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
            ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- 2015, c. 36, s. 79(1). A compassionate care period that had begun but not ended before January 3, 2016: sections 12 and 23.1
-- as they read on that day apply to the claimant from that day.
@export Do sections 12 and 23.1 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to my compassionate care benefits from that day (2015, c. 36, s. 79(1))?
GIVEN `my compassionate care period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which compassionate care benefits could be paid to you begin?
      `my compassionate care period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 12 and 23.1 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to my compassionate care benefits from that day` IS
    `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79(1) sections 12 and 23.1 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to the claimant from that day` (`Period of days` OF `my compassionate care period began on`, `my compassionate care period ended on`)

-- 2015, c. 36, s. 79(2). The same for a self-employed person: sections 152.06 and 152.14.
@export Do sections 152.06 and 152.14 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to my compassionate care benefits as a self-employed person from that day (2015, c. 36, s. 79(2))?
GIVEN `my compassionate care period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which compassionate care benefits could be paid to you as a self-employed person begin?
      `my compassionate care period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 152.06 and 152.14 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to my compassionate care benefits as a self-employed person from that day` IS
    `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79(2) sections 152.06 and 152.14 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to the self-employed person from that day` (`Period of days` OF `my compassionate care period began on`, `my compassionate care period ended on`)

§§ `Which version of the Act governs my benefit period, claim or week (amendments of 2016 to 2022)`

-- SITUATION: your benefit period began, or you made a claim, in 2017 to 2022. For a benefit period that begins today the
-- newer text applies and the lists below are empty.

-- 2016, c. 7, s. 225. The earlier text of three provisions continues to apply to a benefit period that began before
-- July 9, 2017 and had not ended before that day.
@export Which provisions of the Act as they read before July 9, 2017 still govern my benefit period (2016, c. 7, s. 225)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Which provisions of the Act as they read before July 9, 2017 still govern my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 the provisions whose earlier text continues to apply` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`)

-- 2016, c. 7, s. 226. Four provisions apply only to a benefit period that begins on or after a day fixed by order.
@export Which provisions enacted in 2016 apply to my benefit period (2016, c. 7, s. 226)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `the day fixed by order under subsection 231(3) of the 2016 Act is` IS A DATE @desc What is the day fixed by the order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3) of 2016, c. 7? (the order fixes it; the day is not in the text of the Employment Insurance Act)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Which provisions enacted in 2016 apply to my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 226 the provisions that apply as enacted` `my benefit period began on` `the day fixed by order under subsection 231(3) of the 2016 Act is`

-- 2016, c. 7, s. 227. The earlier waiting period provisions continue to apply to a benefit period that began before a day
-- fixed by order.
@export Which waiting period provisions of the Act as they read before the 2016 changes still govern my benefit period (2016, c. 7, s. 227)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `the day fixed by order under subsection 231(4) of the 2016 Act is` IS A DATE @desc What is the day fixed by the order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4) of 2016, c. 7? (the order fixes it; the day is not in the text of the Employment Insurance Act)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Which waiting period provisions of the Act as they read before the 2016 changes still govern my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 227 the provisions whose earlier text continues to apply` `my benefit period began on` `the day fixed by order under subsection 231(4) of the 2016 Act is`

-- 2017, c. 20, s. 254. The earlier Act continues to apply to parental benefits (sections 23 and 152.05) for a child born or
-- placed with the claimant for adoption before the day sections 235 and 245 came into force.
@export Does the Act as it read before the 2017 changes still govern my parental benefits (2017, c. 20, s. 254)?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1 (answer no for a regular claim under Part I)?
      `I am claiming because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim because you are caring for a new-born child or a child placed with you for adoption?
      `my child was born or placed with me for adoption on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your child born or placed with you for adoption (for more than one child, the first of them)?
      `sections 235 and 245 of the 2017 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 235 and 245 of 2017, c. 20 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act as it read before the 2017 changes still govern my parental benefits` IS
    `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 254 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23 or 152.05` `my Part` `my reason` `my child was born or placed with me for adoption on` `sections 235 and 245 of the 2017 Act came into force on`
    WHERE
        `my Part` MEANS IF `I am a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1` THEN `Part VII.1` ELSE `Part I`
        `my reason` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child`
            THEN `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
            ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- 2017, c. 20, s. 255. The earlier Act continues to apply to benefits for a critically ill child (sections 23.2 and 152.061) if
-- the period under 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) begins before the day sections 237 and 247 came into force.
@export Does the Act as it read before the 2017 changes still govern my benefits for caring for a critically ill child (2017, c. 20, s. 255)?
GIVEN `I am claiming because I am caring for a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim because you are providing care or support to a critically ill child?
      `my period for those benefits began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which those benefits could be paid to you begin?
      `sections 237 and 247 of the 2017 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 237 and 247 of 2017, c. 20 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act as it read before the 2017 changes still govern my benefits for caring for a critically ill child` IS
    `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 255 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061` `my reason` `my period for those benefits began on` `sections 237 and 247 of the 2017 Act came into force on`
    WHERE
        `my reason` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming because I am caring for a critically ill child`
            THEN `care or support of a critically ill child`
            ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- 2017, c. 20, s. 256. Sections 23.3 and 152.062 (care of a critically ill adult) apply to a benefit period that begins on or
-- after the day sections 238 and 248 came into force, and, for one not yet ended on that day, to the weeks that begin on or after it.
@export Do the sections on a critically ill adult apply to this week of my benefit period (2017, c. 20, s. 256)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week you are asking about begin?
      `sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sections 238 and 248 of 2017, c. 20 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 23.3 and 152.062 apply to this week of my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 256 sections 23.3 and 152.062 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) `the week I am asking about began on` `sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act came into force on`

-- 2018, c. 27, s. 307. As s. 254 of the 2017 Act, for the day section 307 itself came into force.
@export Does the Act as it read before the 2018 changes still govern my parental benefits (2018, c. 27, s. 307)?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1 (answer no for a regular claim under Part I)?
      `I am claiming because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim because you are caring for a new-born child or a child placed with you for adoption?
      `my child was born or placed with me for adoption on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your child born or placed with you for adoption (for more than one child, the first of them)?
      `section 307 of the 2018 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 307 of 2018, c. 27 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act as it read before the 2018 changes still govern my parental benefits` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 27 s. 307 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23 or 152.05` `my Part` `my reason` `my child was born or placed with me for adoption on` `section 307 of the 2018 Act came into force on`
    WHERE
        `my Part` MEANS IF `I am a self-employed person claiming under Part VII.1` THEN `Part VII.1` ELSE `Part I`
        `my reason` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child`
            THEN `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
            ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- 2020, c. 5, s. 60. Section 58, as it read before the day fixed under section 61, continues to apply to a claimant whose
-- benefit period begins before that day.
@export Does section 58 as it read before the day fixed under section 61 still govern my claim (2020, c. 5, s. 60)?
