§§ `Special situations: Pilot Project No. 10, weeks combined outside Canada, military parental leave and premium rates`

-- SITUATION: you were in Pilot Project No. 10 in March 2009; you are outside Canada and combining weeks of benefits; your parental
-- leave was deferred or you were directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act; or you ask about a premium rate of
-- 2002, 2003 or 2005.

-- 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2). For a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10 whose benefit period had not ended before the second Sunday before
-- royal assent, the maximum number of weeks is determined by Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1) of that Act.
@export Is the maximum number of weeks of benefits for me set by Schedule I as enacted in 2009 (2009, c. 2, s. 226(2))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you included in Pilot Project No. 10?
      `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2009, c. 2 receive royal assent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the maximum number of weeks for me set by Schedule I as enacted in 2009` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the maximum number of weeks is determined under Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1)` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 10` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) `the 2009 Act received royal assent on`

-- 2009, c. 2, s. 229. Subsection 224(1) applies to a claimant whose benefit period had not ended before the day it came into force and
-- did not begin after September 11, 2010.
@export Does subsection 224(1) of the 2009 Act apply to my benefit period (2009, c. 2, s. 229)?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `subsection 224(1) of the 2009 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 224(1) of 2009, c. 2 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does subsection 224(1) of the 2009 Act apply to my benefit period` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) `subsection 224(1) of the 2009 Act came into force on`

-- 2009, c. 30, s. 7. Regulation 55(10) is deemed to read differently for a claimant to whom any of sections 3 to 6 of that Act applies
-- and whose benefit period has not been extended under 10(13) to (13.3).
@export Is subsection 55(10) of the Employment Insurance Regulations deemed to read differently for me (2009, c. 30, s. 7)?
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30 apply to you?
      `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 10(13), (13.1), (13.2) or (13.3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is subsection 55(10) of the Regulations deemed to read differently for me` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to me` `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 10(13), (13.1), (13.2) or (13.3)`

@export How many weeks of benefits may I combine while I am outside Canada (2009, c. 30, s. 7)?
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30 apply to you?
      `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 10(13), (13.1), (13.2) or (13.3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)?
      `I am not in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you outside Canada?
      `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are you entitled to?
      `the most I may be paid under paragraphs 55(7)(a) and (b) of the Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 55(7)(a) and (b) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 is` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to you under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits may I combine while I am outside Canada` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to me` `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 10(13), (13.1), (13.2) or (13.3)` `I am not in Canada` `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Regulations` `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to` `the most I may be paid under paragraphs 55(7)(a) and (b) of the Regulations` `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 is`

-- 2010, c. 9, s. 4(1). Sections 2 and 3 of that Act apply to a claimant whose benefit period began less than 104 weeks before the day it
-- came into force, if the period under 23(2) had not ended before that day, or had ended and the parental leave had been deferred (or a
-- return to duty directed) and the deferral had not ended before that day.
@export Do sections 2 and 3 of the 2010 Act apply to me (2010, c. 9, s. 4(1))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which parental benefits could be paid to you under subsection 23(2) begin?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within that period, was your parental leave deferred, or were you directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act?
      `my deferral or return to duty ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the deferral or return to duty end (answer any day if none applies)?
      `the 2010 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2010, c. 9 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 2 and 3 of the 2010 Act apply to me` IS
    `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) (`Period of days` OF `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on`, `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on`) `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` `my deferral or return to duty ended on` `the 2010 Act came into force on`

-- 2010, c. 9, s. 4(2). The 23(2) period is extended to 104 weeks. The answer is the last day of the extended period, or nothing if the
-- subsection does not extend it.
@export Until what day is my period for parental benefits extended under subsection 4(2) of the 2010 Act (2010, c. 9, s. 4(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end (or on what day is it due to end)?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which parental benefits could be paid to you under subsection 23(2) begin?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period end?
      `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within that period, was your parental leave deferred, or were you directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act?
      `my deferral or return to duty ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the deferral or return to duty end?
      `the 2010 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2010, c. 9 come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until what day is my period for parental benefits extended under subsection 4(2) of the 2010 Act` IS
    `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the last day of the period as extended to 104 weeks` `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on` (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) (`Period of days` OF `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on`, `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on`) `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` `my deferral or return to duty ended on` `the 2010 Act came into force on`)

-- 2010, c. 9, s. 4(3). The benefit period and the 23(2) period are each extended to 104 weeks. The answer is the last day of the
-- extended benefit period, or nothing if the subsection does not extend it.
@export Until what day is my benefit period extended under subsection 4(3) of the 2010 Act (2010, c. 9, s. 4(3))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period end?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period in which parental benefits could be paid to you under subsection 23(2) begin?
      `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period end?
      `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within that period, was your parental leave deferred, or were you directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act?
      `my deferral or return to duty ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the deferral or return to duty end?
      `the 2010 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2010, c. 9 come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until what day is my benefit period extended under subsection 4(3) of the 2010 Act` IS
    `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the last day of the period as extended to 104 weeks` `my benefit period began on` (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`) (`Period of days` OF `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) began on`, `my period for parental benefits under subsection 23(2) ended on`) `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act` `my deferral or return to duty ended on` `the 2010 Act came into force on`)

-- 2009, c. 2, ss. 227 and 228. The premium rate for 2002 (2.2%), 2003 (2.1%) and 2005 (1.95%) is the rate the deemed sections state.
-- For any other year the sections say nothing and section 66 governs.
@export What premium rate did sections 66.1 and 66.3 set for this year (2009, c. 2, ss. 227 and 228)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about is` IS A NUMBER @desc Which year are you asking about (for example 2002)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What premium rate did sections 66.1 and 66.3 set for this year` IS
    CONSIDER `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` `the year I am asking about is`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST rate
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 228 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.3` `the year I am asking about is`

§§ `Self-employed persons: agreements and violations (2009)`

-- SITUATION: you are, or were, a self-employed person who entered into an agreement with the Commission under subsection 152.02(1)
-- in 2009 or 2010, or who was given a notice of violation under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force.

-- 2009, c. 33, s. 18. An agreement under subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into from the day the 2009 Act received royal assent to the
-- day section 16 came into force.
@export May I enter into an agreement under subsection 152.02(1) on this day (2009, c. 33, s. 18)?
GIVEN `the day I would enter into the agreement is` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you enter into, or did you enter into, the agreement?
      `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2009, c. 33 receive royal assent?
      `section 16 of the 2009 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 16 of 2009, c. 33 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I enter into an agreement under subsection 152.02(1) on this day` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` `the day I would enter into the agreement is` `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` `section 16 of the 2009 Act came into force on`

@export On what day is my agreement under subsection 152.02(1) treated as entered into (2009, c. 33, s. 18)?
GIVEN `the day I entered into the agreement is` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter into the agreement?
      `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2009, c. 33 receive royal assent?
      `section 16 of the 2009 Act came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 16 of 2009, c. 33 come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my agreement under subsection 152.02(1) treated as entered into` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 the day on which the agreement is deemed to have been entered into` `the day I entered into the agreement is` `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` `section 16 of the 2009 Act came into force on`

-- 2009, c. 33, s. 19. Despite paragraph 152.07(1)(a), a Part VII.1 benefit period may begin on or after January 1, 2011 if the agreement was
-- entered into from the later of royal assent and January 1, 2010 to April 1, 2010.
@export May my benefit period under Part VII.1 begin on or after January 1, 2011 although fewer than 12 months have passed since my agreement (2009, c. 33, s. 19)?
GIVEN `my benefit period would begin on` IS A DATE @desc On what day would your benefit period under Part VII.1 begin?
      `the day I entered into the agreement is` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter into the agreement under subsection 152.02(1)?
      `the 2009 Act received royal assent on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did 2009, c. 33 receive royal assent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my benefit period under Part VII.1 begin on or after January 1, 2011 although fewer than 12 months have passed since my agreement` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` `my benefit period would begin on` `the day I entered into the agreement is` `the 2009 Act received royal assent on`

-- 2009, c. 33, s. 20. A violation accumulated under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force is treated as accumulated
-- under section 152.07 on the day the notice of violation was given.
@export On what day is a violation I was given notice of treated as accumulated under section 152.07 (2009, c. 33, s. 20)?
GIVEN `the violation was accumulated under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the violation accumulated under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force?
      `I was given the notice of violation on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of violation given to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is a violation I was given notice of treated as accumulated under section 152.07` IS
    `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 20 the day on which the violation is deemed to have been accumulated under section 152.07` `the violation was accumulated under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force` `I was given the notice of violation on`

§§ `Electing a different deduction of earnings (2018, c. 12, ss. 292 to 295)`

-- SITUATION: you were a claimant before August 15, 2021 and had earnings in a week of unemployment; you made, or could have made, an
-- election under section 77.98 or 77.991 of the Employment Insurance Regulations (as they read on August 11, 2018) about how earnings
-- are deducted from your benefits.

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(1). A claimant who was eligible to elect under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations and did not before August 12,
-- 2018 may, after August 11, 2018, elect under s. 293(2) if the last notification for the benefit period was issued after July 13, 2018
-- and the claimant received earnings in a week of unemployment in it and claimed for at least one such week.
@export May I elect to have my earnings deducted by the measure in section 293 (2018, c. 12, s. 293(1))?
GIVEN `I was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations for this benefit period?
      `I made such an election before August 12, 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make such an election before August 12, 2018?
      `I make the election on` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make, or did you make, the election?
      `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
      `I received earnings in one or more weeks of unemployment in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment in this benefit period?
      `I made a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I elect to have my earnings deducted by the measure in section 293` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) the claimant may make an election under subsection (2)` `I was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` `I made such an election before August 12, 2018` `I make the election on` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` `I received earnings in one or more weeks of unemployment in the benefit period` `I made a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(2). If the claimant elects, the amount of the week's earnings that exceeds $75 (rate under $188) or 40% of the weekly
-- rate (rate $188 or more) is deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2).
@export How much of my earnings for the week is deducted if I elect under section 293 (2018, c. 12, s. 293(2))?
GIVEN `I was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations for this benefit period?
      `I made such an election before August 12, 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make such an election before August 12, 2018?
      `I make the election on` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make, or did you make, the election?
      `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
      `I received earnings in one or more weeks of unemployment in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment in this benefit period?
      `I made a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks?
      `I elect to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect to have the amount in section 293(2) deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2)?
      `my earnings for the week were` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your earnings for the week of unemployment, in dollars?
      `my rate of weekly benefits is` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my earnings for the week is deducted if I elect under section 293` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) the amount of the week's earnings deducted under the election` `I was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` `I made such an election before August 12, 2018` `I make the election on` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` `I received earnings in one or more weeks of unemployment in the benefit period` `I made a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks` `I elect to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2)` `my earnings for the week were` `my rate of weekly benefits is`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(3). The claimant must inform the Commission not later than the 30th day after the day the last notification was issued.
@export By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under section 293 (2018, c. 12, s. 293(3))?
GIVEN `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under section 293` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(3) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of the election` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(3). The election is irrevocable.
@export May I take back my election under section 293 (2018, c. 12, s. 293(3))?
GIVEN `I have made the election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under section 293?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take back my election under section 293` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(3) the claimant may revoke the election` `I have made the election`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(3), (4). In time if told by the 30th day; if later, treated as in time if the claimant shows good cause for the delay
-- for every day from the deadline to the day told. Whether good cause is shown is the Commission's judgment.
@export Is my election under section 293 treated as made in time (2018, c. 12, s. 293(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
      `I told the Commission of my election on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you tell the Commission of your election?
      `I can show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the deadline to the day I told the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that there was good cause for the delay on every day from the deadline until the day you told the Commission? (the Commission decides whether you have shown it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election under section 293 treated as made in time` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(3), (4) the election is treated as made by the deadline` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` `I told the Commission of my election on` `I can show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the deadline to the day I told the Commission`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 293(5). A decision of the Commission about an election, including a failure to make one, is not subject to
-- reconsideration under section 112.
@export Can the Commission's decision about my election under section 293 be reconsidered under section 112 (2018, c. 12, s. 293(5))?
GIVEN `the decision is about an election, including my failure to make one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission's decision in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission's decision about my election under section 293 be reconsidered under section 112` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(5) the decision of the Commission is subject to reconsideration under section 112` `the decision is about an election, including my failure to make one`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 294. An election made before August 12, 2018 under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations is deemed to apply to earnings
-- received in all weeks of unemployment in the part of the benefit period that falls from August 12, 2018 to August 14, 2021.
@export Does my earlier election apply to my earnings for this week (2018, c. 12, s. 294)?
GIVEN `I made my election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make your election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the week is a week of unemployment in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week a week of unemployment included in the benefit period?
      `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week you are asking about begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my earlier election apply to my earnings for this week` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 294 the earlier election is deemed to apply to the earnings received during the week` `I made my election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations on` `the week is a week of unemployment in my benefit period` `the week I am asking about began on`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 295(1). The section applies to a claimant who made a 77.98 election (last notification after August 6, 2016), or a
-- 77.991(2) election, or who makes an election under section 293.
@export Does section 295 apply to me (2018, c. 12, s. 295(1))?
GIVEN `I made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations for the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an election under section 77.98 of the Employment Insurance Regulations for this benefit period?
      `the last notification for that benefit period was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for that benefit period issued to you?
      `I made an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `I make an election under section 293` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an election under section 293?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 295 apply to me` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(1) section 295 applies to the claimant` `I made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations for the benefit period` `the last notification for that benefit period was issued to me on` `I made an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` `I make an election under section 293`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 295(2). For a benefit period established after August 11, 2018 but before August 15, 2021, and weeks before August 15, 2021,
-- the amount of the week's earnings above $75 (or 40% of the rate) is deducted instead of the amount under 19(2) or 152.18(2).
@export How much of my earnings for the week is deducted if I elect under section 295 (2018, c. 12, s. 295(2))?
GIVEN `section 295 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 295 apply to you (see the question "Does section 295 apply to me")?
      `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established?
      `the week I am asking about began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week of unemployment you are asking about begin?
      `I elect to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect to have the amount in section 295(2) deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2)?
      `my earnings for the week were` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your earnings for the week of unemployment, in dollars?
      `my rate of weekly benefits is` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my earnings for the week is deducted if I elect under section 295` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(2) the amount of the week's earnings deducted under the election` `section 295 applies to me` `my benefit period was established on` `the week I am asking about began on` `I elect to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2)` `my earnings for the week were` `my rate of weekly benefits is`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 295(3). Not later than the 30th day after the day the last notification was issued, or February 19, 2022, whichever is earlier.
@export By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under section 295 (2018, c. 12, s. 295(3))?
GIVEN `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under section 295` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(3) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of the election` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on`

@export May I take back my election under section 295 (2018, c. 12, s. 295(3))?
GIVEN `I have made the election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under section 295?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take back my election under section 295` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(3) the claimant may revoke the election` `I have made the election`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 295(3), (4). As for section 293.
@export Is my election under section 295 treated as made in time (2018, c. 12, s. 295(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for this benefit period issued to you?
      `I told the Commission of my election on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you tell the Commission of your election?
      `I can show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the deadline to the day I told the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that there was good cause for the delay on every day from the deadline until the day you told the Commission? (the Commission decides whether you have shown it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election under section 295 treated as made in time` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(3), (4) the election is treated as made by the deadline` `the last notification of payment or non-payment was issued to me on` `I told the Commission of my election on` `I can show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the deadline to the day I told the Commission`

-- 2018, c. 12, s. 295(5). As s. 293(5).
@export Can the Commission's decision about my election under section 295 be reconsidered under section 112 (2018, c. 12, s. 295(5))?
GIVEN `the decision is about an election, including my failure to make one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission's decision in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission's decision about my election under section 295 be reconsidered under section 112` IS
    `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(5) the decision of the Commission is subject to reconsideration under section 112` `the decision is about an election, including my failure to make one`

§§ `Appeals and requests for reconsideration that were pending on April 1, 2013 (2012, c. 19, ss. 265 to 270)`

-- SITUATION: you had an appeal to a board of referees or an umpire, or a request for reconsideration under the old section 120, that was
-- filed before April 1, 2013 and had not been decided by then.

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 252. The Pension Appeals Board, a Review Tribunal, a board of referees or an umpire must transfer to the Social Security
-- Tribunal any information under their control that relates to an application the Tribunal is seized of, or that the Governor in Council
-- has by regulation prescribed. The four bodies are treated alike by the section, so one yes-or-no answers for all of them.
@export Must the body that dealt with my case transfer information about it to the Social Security Tribunal (2012, c. 19, s. 252)?
GIVEN `the body is the Pension Appeals Board, a Review Tribunal, a board of referees or an umpire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body that holds the information the Pension Appeals Board, a Review Tribunal, a board of referees or an umpire?
      `the information relates to an application of which the Social Security Tribunal is seized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to an application of which the Social Security Tribunal is seized?
      `the Governor in Council has prescribed the information by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Governor in Council, by regulation, prescribed the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the body that dealt with my case transfer information about it to the Social Security Tribunal` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 252 the body must transfer the information to the Social Security Tribunal` `the body` `the information relates to an application of which the Social Security Tribunal is seized` `the Governor in Council has prescribed the information by regulation`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the section treats the four bodies alike, so any one of them stands for all; a body outside the four is the Tribunal itself.
        `the body` MEANS
            IF `the body is the Pension Appeals Board, a Review Tribunal, a board of referees or an umpire`
            THEN `ei7 the board of referees`
            ELSE `ei7 the Social Security Tribunal`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 265(1). The board of referees remains seized of an appeal filed under the old subsection 114(1) and not decided before
-- April 1, 2013.
@export Is my appeal filed before April 1, 2013 still before the board of referees (2012, c. 19, s. 265(1))?
GIVEN `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 114(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal filed under subsection 114(1) of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `my appeal was filed on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal filed?
      `my appeal was decided before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal decided before April 1, 2013?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my appeal filed before April 1, 2013 still before the board of referees` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(1) the board of referees remains seized of the appeal` `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 114(1)` `my appeal was filed on` `my appeal was decided before April 1, 2013`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 265(2). The board must decide no later than October 31, 2013 or, if an order is made under subsection 263(4), the day
-- before the day fixed by that order.
@export By what day must the board of referees decide my appeal (2012, c. 19, s. 265(2))?
GIVEN `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under subsection 263(4) of 2012, c. 19 fixing an earlier day than November 1, 2013?
      `the day fixed by that order is` IS A DATE @desc What is the day fixed by that order (answer any day if there was no order)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the board of referees decide my appeal` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(2) the last day on which the board of referees must make its decision` `the order day`
    WHERE
        `the order day` MEANS IF `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` THEN JUST `the day fixed by that order is` ELSE NOTHING

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 265(3). If the board has not decided by that day, the General Division becomes seized of the appeal.
@export Which body becomes seized of my appeal if the board of referees has not decided it in time (2012, c. 19, s. 265(3))?
GIVEN `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 114(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal filed under subsection 114(1) of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `my appeal was filed on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal filed?
      `my appeal was decided before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal decided before April 1, 2013?
      `the board of referees has decided my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of referees decided your appeal?
      `the board of referees decided my appeal on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the board of referees decide your appeal (answer any day if it has not)?
      `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under subsection 263(4) of 2012, c. 19 fixing an earlier day than November 1, 2013?
      `the day fixed by that order is` IS A DATE @desc What is the day fixed by that order (answer any day if there was no order)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Which body becomes seized of my appeal if the board of referees has not decided it in time` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) the body that becomes seized of the appeal` `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 114(1)` `my appeal was filed on` `my appeal was decided before April 1, 2013` `the day of decision` `the order day`
    WHERE
        `the day of decision` MEANS IF `the board of referees has decided my appeal` THEN JUST `the board of referees decided my appeal on` ELSE NOTHING
        `the order day` MEANS IF `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` THEN JUST `the day fixed by that order is` ELSE NOTHING

@export On what day is my appeal treated as filed with the General Division (2012, c. 19, s. 265(3))?
GIVEN `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under subsection 263(4) of 2012, c. 19 fixing an earlier day than November 1, 2013?
      `the day fixed by that order is` IS A DATE @desc What is the day fixed by that order (answer any day if there was no order)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my appeal treated as filed with the General Division` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) the day on which the appeal is deemed to have been filed with the General Division` `the order day`
    WHERE
        `the order day` MEANS IF `an order under subsection 263(4) fixed the day` THEN JUST `the day fixed by that order is` ELSE NOTHING

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 265(4). A person dissatisfied with a decision made under subsection (1) may appeal it to the Appeal Division.
@export May I appeal the board of referees' decision to the Appeal Division (2012, c. 19, s. 265(4))?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision?
      `the decision was made by the board of referees under subsection 265(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made by the board of referees in an appeal it remained seized of under subsection 265(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `May I appeal the board of referees' decision to the Appeal Division` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(4) the body to which the person may appeal the decision` `I am dissatisfied with the decision` `the decision was made by the board of referees under subsection 265(1)`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 266. An appeal from a board of referees' decision that could have been appealed to an umpire, but for the repeal of 115(1),
-- may be appealed to the Appeal Division.
@export May I appeal a board of referees' decision that could have gone to an umpire to the Appeal Division (2012, c. 19, s. 266)?
GIVEN `it is an appeal from a decision of a board of referees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal from a decision of a board of referees?
      `it could have been appealed to an umpire but for the repeal of subsection 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could it have been appealed to an umpire but for the repeal of subsection 115(1) of the Act by section 247 of 2012, c. 19?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `May I appeal a board of referees' decision that could have gone to an umpire to the Appeal Division` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 266 the body to which the appeal may be appealed` `it is an appeal from a decision of a board of referees` `it could have been appealed to an umpire but for the repeal of subsection 115(1)`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 267(1). An umpire remains seized of an appeal filed and heard before April 1, 2013 under the old subsection 115(1).
@export Is my appeal to an umpire, filed and heard before April 1, 2013, still before the umpire (2012, c. 19, s. 267(1))?
GIVEN `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal filed under subsection 115(1) of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `my appeal was filed on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal filed?
      `my appeal has been heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your appeal been heard?
      `my appeal was heard on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal heard (answer any day if it has not been heard)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my appeal to an umpire, filed and heard before April 1, 2013, still before the umpire` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(1) the umpire remains seized of the appeal` `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` `my appeal was filed on` `the day heard`
    WHERE
        `the day heard` MEANS IF `my appeal has been heard` THEN JUST `my appeal was heard on` ELSE NOTHING

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 267(2) and (3). The umpire must decide no later than March 31, 2014; if no decision has been made by then, the Appeal
-- Division becomes seized and is deemed to have granted leave to appeal on April 1, 2014.
@export By what day must the umpire decide my appeal (2012, c. 19, s. 267(2))?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the umpire decide my appeal` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(2) the last day on which the umpire must make the decision`

@export Does the Appeal Division become seized of my appeal because the umpire did not decide it in time (2012, c. 19, s. 267(3))?
GIVEN `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal filed under subsection 115(1) of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `my appeal was filed on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal filed?
      `my appeal has been heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your appeal been heard?
      `my appeal was heard on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal heard (answer any day if it has not been heard)?
      `the umpire has decided my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the umpire decided your appeal?
      `the umpire decided my appeal on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the umpire decide your appeal (answer any day if not decided)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Appeal Division become seized of my appeal because the umpire did not decide it in time` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) the Appeal Division becomes seized of the appeal` `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` `my appeal was filed on` `the day heard` `the day decided`
    WHERE
        `the day heard` MEANS IF `my appeal has been heard` THEN JUST `my appeal was heard on` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day decided` MEANS IF `the umpire has decided my appeal` THEN JUST `the umpire decided my appeal on` ELSE NOTHING

@export On what day is leave to appeal treated as granted to me by the Appeal Division after the umpire missed his or her deadline (2012, c. 19, s. 267(3))?
GIVEN `the Appeal Division has become seized of my appeal under subsection 267(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Appeal Division become seized of your appeal because the umpire made no decision by March 31, 2014?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is leave to appeal treated as granted to me by the Appeal Division after the umpire missed the deadline` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) the day on which the Appeal Division is deemed to have granted leave to appeal` `the Appeal Division has become seized of my appeal under subsection 267(3)`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 268. For an appeal filed and not heard before April 1, 2013 under the old subsection 115(1), the Appeal Division is deemed to
-- have granted leave to appeal on April 1, 2013.
@export On what day is leave to appeal treated as granted to me for an appeal not heard before April 1, 2013 (2012, c. 19, s. 268)?
GIVEN `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal filed under subsection 115(1) of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `my appeal was filed on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your appeal filed?
      `my appeal was heard before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your appeal heard before April 1, 2013?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is leave to appeal treated as granted to me for an appeal not heard before April 1, 2013` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 268 the day on which the Appeal Division is deemed to have granted leave to appeal` `my appeal was filed under the old subsection 115(1)` `my appeal was filed on` `my appeal was heard before April 1, 2013`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 269(1). A request for reconsideration under the old section 120 on which no decision had been made before April 1, 2013 is
-- deemed an application made on April 1, 2013 under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act.
@export On what day is my request for reconsideration treated as an application under section 66 (2012, c. 19, s. 269(1))?
GIVEN `I made a request under the old section 120` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a request for reconsideration under section 120 of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `a decision was made on my request before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a decision made on your request before April 1, 2013?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my request for reconsideration treated as an application under section 66` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(1) the day on which the request is deemed to have been made as an application under section 66` `I made a request under the old section 120` `a decision was made on my request before April 1, 2013`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 269(1)(a), (b). The application is deemed to relate to a decision of the General Division if the decision was a board of
-- referees', and of the Appeal Division if it was an umpire's.
@export Whose decision does my request treated as an application relate to (2012, c. 19, s. 269(1))?
GIVEN `I made a request under the old section 120` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a request for reconsideration under section 120 of the Act as it read before section 247 of 2012, c. 19 came into force?
      `a decision was made on my request before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a decision made on your request before April 1, 2013?
      `the decision being reconsidered was made by a board of referees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision you asked to have reconsidered made by a board of referees (answer no if it was made by an umpire)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Whose decision does my request treated as an application relate to` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(1) the division whose decision the deemed application relates to` `I made a request under the old section 120` `a decision was made on my request before April 1, 2013` `the body that made the decision`
    WHERE
        `the body that made the decision` MEANS
            IF `the decision being reconsidered was made by a board of referees`
            THEN `ei7 the board of referees`
            ELSE `ei7 an umpire`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 269(2). An application under section 66 made after March 31, 2013 is deemed to relate to a decision of the General Division
-- (a board of referees' decision) or of the Appeal Division (an umpire's).
@export Whose decision does my application under section 66 made after March 31, 2013 relate to (2012, c. 19, s. 269(2))?
GIVEN `I made my application on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make your application under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act?
      `the decision concerned was made by a board of referees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision your application concerns made by a board of referees (answer no if it was made by an umpire)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Whose decision does my application under section 66 made after March 31, 2013 relate to` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(2) the division whose decision the application is deemed to relate to` `I made my application on` `the body that made the decision`
    WHERE
        `the body that made the decision` MEANS
            IF `the decision concerned was made by a board of referees`
            THEN `ei7 the board of referees`
            ELSE `ei7 an umpire`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 270. The provisions repealed by that Act, and their related regulations, continue to apply to appeals the board of referees or an
-- umpire remains seized of.
@export Do the repealed provisions of the Act still apply to my appeal (2012, c. 19, s. 270)?
GIVEN `the board of referees or an umpire remains seized of my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the board of referees or an umpire remain seized of your appeal under 2012, c. 19?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the repealed provisions of the Act still apply to my appeal` IS
    `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 270 the provisions repealed by that Act and their related regulations continue to apply to the appeal` `the board of referees or an umpire remains seized of my appeal`

§§ `Section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act (2023, c. 26, s. 676)`

-- SITUATION: you have a decision, or an ongoing application, under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in
-- relation to the Employment Insurance Act.

-- 2023, c. 26, s. 676(1), (2).
@export Does section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 stay out of my decision or application under section 66 (2023, c. 26, s. 676(1))?
GIVEN `I have a decision under the earlier section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read before Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 came into force?
      `I have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act?
      `my application was ongoing immediately before section 634 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application ongoing immediately before section 634 of 2023, c. 26 came into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 stay out of my decision or application under section 66` IS
    `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 676(1) section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 does not apply` `I have a decision under the earlier section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` `I have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` `my application was ongoing immediately before section 634 came into force`

@export Is my matter dealt with under section 66 as it read before Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 came into force (2023, c. 26, s. 676(2))?
GIVEN `I have a decision under the earlier section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read before Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 came into force?
      `I have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act?
      `my application was ongoing immediately before section 634 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application ongoing immediately before section 634 of 2023, c. 26 came into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my matter dealt with under section 66 as it read before Division 20 came into force` IS
    `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 676(2) the matter is dealt with in accordance with section 66 as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 comes into force` `I have a decision under the earlier section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` `I have an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` `my application was ongoing immediately before section 634 came into force`

§§ `Interim Orders of 2020`

-- SITUATION: your claim was made while one of the 2020 Interim Orders was in effect.

-- SOR/2020-61, s. 2. The provisions of Part VIII.4 apply despite any other provision of the Act or its regulations.
@export Does Part VIII.4 apply despite a conflicting provision of the Act or the Regulations (SOR/2020-61, s. 2)?
GIVEN `the conflicting provision is a provision of the Act outside Part VIII.4 or of its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision that conflicts with Part VIII.4 a provision of the Employment Insurance Act outside Part VIII.4, or of a regulation made under it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part VIII.4 apply despite a conflicting provision of the Act or the Regulations` IS
    `Act RP SOR/2020-61 s. 2 the provisions of Part VIII.4 apply despite the other provision` `the conflicting provision is a provision of the Act outside Part VIII.4 or of its regulations`

-- SOR/2020-88, -89, -95, -141, -169, -173, -187, -188 and -208. For greater certainty, each Interim Order applies despite any provision of the Act
-- or its regulations.
@export Does one of the 2020 Interim Orders apply despite a conflicting provision of the Act or the Regulations (SOR/2020-88 and eight others)?
GIVEN `the order is one of the Interim Orders SOR/2020-88, -89, -95, -141, -169, -173, -187, -188 and -208` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one of the Interim Orders SOR/2020-88, SOR/2020-89, SOR/2020-95, SOR/2020-141, SOR/2020-169, SOR/2020-173, SOR/2020-187, SOR/2020-188 and SOR/2020-208?
      `the conflicting provision is a provision of the Act or of its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision that conflicts with the order a provision of the Employment Insurance Act or of a regulation made under it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does one of the 2020 Interim Orders apply despite a conflicting provision of the Act or the Regulations` IS
    `Act RP nine Interim Orders of 2020 the Interim Order applies despite the other provision` `the order is one of the Interim Orders SOR/2020-88, -89, -95, -141, -169, -173, -187, -188 and -208` `the conflicting provision is a provision of the Act or of its regulations`
